Step-by-step roadmap
Baseline scaffolding (Day 0)

Add src/constraints/base.py with an abstract Constraint class (name, category, priority, apply(context), metadata).
Create package layout: constraints/lab, constraints/theory, constraints/cross_system, constraints/utility, and drop __init__.py files plus docstrings describing expected constraint bundles.
Extend constraints/registry.py to load constraint classes dynamically and expose ConstraintSpec (id, factory, priority, enabled flag, weight).
Quick test: python -m compileall src/constraints and a tiny unit test that instantiates a dummy constraint to ensure the base & registry wiring works.
Constraint context + helpers

Define a ConstraintContext dataclass (or reuse ModelBuilder’s version) that hands each constraint the OR-Tools model, variables, ExtendedDataContainer, configuration, and logging/tracing hooks.
Provide shared helper mixins/utilities (e.g., lab session iterators, room lookups) in constraints/utils.py to avoid duplication later.
Quick test: Add unit tests ensuring helpers return expected slot/group sets using a mini fixture.
Lab phase 1 – coverage & requirements

Files: lab/requirements.py (ensure each lab group meets required weekly count) and lab/core_lab.py (hard constraints for mapped core labs).
Translate the corresponding logic blocks from combined_scheduler.py into constraint classes with clear apply() steps.
Register them in the registry with priority="hard" and config toggles.
Verification: Write focused tests using a synthetic lab dataset to assert feasibility/infeasibility toggles; run pytest tests/constraints/lab/test_requirements.py.
Lab phase 2 – rooms, capacities, shifts

Implement lab/room_allocation.py, lab/capacity_analysis.py, and lab/shift_based.py.
Include helper data (room capacities, shift windows) pulled from ExtendedDataContainer.
Introduce soft penalties where the legacy code used preference scoring (e.g., capacity slack).
Verification: Add tests for room conflicts and shift violations; also run a smoke ModelBuilder build with only lab constraints to ensure integration still compiles.
Theory phase 1 – group scheduling & teacher presence

Files: theory/group_scheduling.py, theory/teacher_presence.py.
Port logic ensuring theory groups are assigned to valid slots, teachers aren’t double-booked, and that teacher availability windows are respected (including pop.csv preferences).
Verification: Unit tests for no double-booking + optional penalty scoring for preference misses.
Theory phase 2 – room & temporal structure

Files: theory/room_capacity.py, theory/daily_limits.py, theory/consecutive_slots.py.
Capture daily load limits, avoid undesirable consecutive sessions, and enforce room capacity.
Verification: Extend theory test suite; run pytest tests/constraints/theory.
Cross-system constraints

Files: cross_system/teacher_clash.py, cross_system/department_conflicts.py, cross_system/time_mapping.py.
These coordinate lab vs. theory collisions, department-level day assignments, and lab↔theory time mapping (the _build_time_mapping() logic).
Because they touch everything, add integration tests that run ModelBuilder.build() with both lab/theory vars and assert conflict detection works.
Utility/quality-of-life rules

Files: utility/lunch_break.py, utility/five_pm_constraints.py, utility/teacher_preferences.py.
Encode lunch-window protection, 5 PM limits, and softer teacher-day preferences (as penalty terms).
Verification: Unit tests plus regression config ensuring penalties appear in the objective.
Registry finalization + config binding

Populate constraints/registry.py with all constraints, grouped by priority and bound to config keys (e.g., config["constraints"]["lab"]["requirements"]["enabled"]).
Update default config YAMLs (constraint.yaml, etc.) to toggle modules and weights.
Verification: run python -m compileall src + a short script that iterates registry.iter_specs() and instantiates each constraint with a mocked context.
Documentation & tracking

Update outstanding_modules_todo.txt to mark completed submodules and record any deviations.
Add a docs/constraints.md (or extend README) summarizing available constraints, their config toggles, and test coverage.
Verification: CI-style pytest run plus lint/format checks if configured.
Testing cadence
After each package phase (lab1, lab2, theory1, etc.), add/extend targeted pytest modules so regressions are caught early.
Maintain a lightweight integration harness (e.g., tests/integration/test_model_builder_smoke.py) that builds the model with subsets of constraints to ensure the registry wiring remains valid.
Once all constraints are ported, run a full synthetic scheduling scenario and compare outputs against the legacy results for sanity.